instantiations, both twins.

Order-5 K-class `rK = 12` (`|K| = 5`, `|G/K| = 625`).  The `|H| ≤ |K| = 5` and
`t⁻¹Ht = K` pruning leaves exactly **two** nonzero `H`-columns:

* **`H = ⊥`** (`rH = 0`): `(G/K)^⊥ = G/K`, so `φ_{⊥,1}[K,λ] = |G/K| = 625` for every
  `λ` — proven **abstractly** (`species_one_basisElt` + `card_fixedPoints_bot`), no
  625-coset transversal decide;
* **`H = K`** (`rH = 12`): the diagonal column, `|T(K,K)| = 625`, landed via the
  emitted fixed sub-transversal and the `LeanDring/P5/Certificate/SpeciesTable/EntryTransA.lean` adapters.

The full 625-coset transversal `R12` is embedded once (its `reduceAux`-proxy
injectivity is the one heavy per-`rK` decide, feeding the `H = K` `hcard`).
Transversal data is SHARED byte-identically between the twins (verified in the
emitter; re-checked by the q=2 `decide`s).
-/

